        "content": "<p>fitzgen opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15241\">PR #15241</a> from <code>fitzgen:do-not-hoist-out-of-cold-blocks</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It likely is moving the value's computation out of a rare cold path and into a less-rare, hotter path.</p>\n<p>This improves the code generated for the <code>sync-adapter-lazy-lend-in-loop.wat</code> disas test, but doesn't actually show a speed up to the <code>cm-online-stats</code> benchmark that that disas test is a rough proxy for. Presumably because, even though the cold path is never taken in that benchmark and so hoisting causes instructions that would not previously have been run to be executed, they are executed only once in the loop pre-header so the total delta instructions for the whole benchmark run is a tiny handful.</p>\n<p>On the full Sightglass suite, this is a very small improvement to a number of benchmarks:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">compilation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">instructions</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">retired</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Geomean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">29</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">benchmarks</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">No</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">difference</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">performance</span><span class=\"p\">.</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">┌──────────────┬────────────┬──────────────────┐</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </s